      en: "Situated in southwestern Serbia near the Studenica River at an altitude of 400 m, the monastery lies in a wooded valley at the foot of Mount Radocelo. The complex covers 1.5 hectares enclosed by 13th-century stone walls. The main church, dedicated to the Virgin, is built of white marble and features a central dome rising 20 m. The surrounding area is characterized by karst landscapes and a continental climate. The nearest town is Raška, 12 km away. The monastery was declared a Monument of Culture of Exceptional Importance in 1947 and is a key stop on the cultural route of medieval Serbian monasteries.",
